Consuming state in components:


- 🔥We can now inject the service in components that need user state. The home component displays
    different templates based on whether a user is logged in.

        @Component({
            selector: 'ns-home',
            imports: [RouterLink],
            template: `
                @if (user(); as user) {
                <div>Greetings, {{ user.name }}!</div>
                } @else {
                <a routerLink="/login">Log in</a>
                }
            `
        })

        export class Home {
            protected readonly user = inject(UserService).currentUser;
        }